\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces One AccidentTwoWays scenario (Route\nobreakspace  {}1105) under UniAD (red) and VAD (blue). UniAD collides with one agent at $t=0.6$\,s ($R=0.962$). VAD never overlaps any agent's box within the 4\,s window, yet closes on another agent from $57.8$\,m to $3.4$\,m and is still approaching at about $4$\,m/s when the window ends ($R=0.975$). (a) Closed-form per-frame risk $r(t)$ (Eq.\nobreakspace  {}\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq:continuous_risk}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}): nonzero for UniAD, zero for VAD. (b1)/(b2) Bird's-eye view of ego and agent paths in each ego's local frame at $t=0$; light boxes mark footprints at $t=0$, solid boxes at the moment of interest (UniAD: contact; VAD: end of window). (c) Critical-event hazard $q_k$ (Eq.\nobreakspace  {}\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq:event_time_distribution}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}) for the agent each case concerns.}}{10}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:case_study_uniad_vs_vad}{{4}{10}{One AccidentTwoWays scenario (Route~1105) under UniAD (red) and VAD (blue). UniAD collides with one agent at $t=0.6$\,s ($R=0.962$). VAD never overlaps any agent's box within the 4\,s window, yet closes on another agent from $57.8$\,m to $3.4$\,m and is still approaching at about $4$\,m/s when the window ends ($R=0.975$). (a) Closed-form per-frame risk $r(t)$ (Eq.~\eqref {eq:continuous_risk}): nonzero for UniAD, zero for VAD. (b1)/(b2) Bird's-eye view of ego and agent paths in each ego's local frame at $t=0$; light boxes mark footprints at $t=0$, solid boxes at the moment of interest (UniAD: contact; VAD: end of window). (c) Critical-event hazard $q_k$ (Eq.~\eqref {eq:event_time_distribution}) for the agent each case concerns}{figure.4}{}}
